/* ============================================================================
polynomial-from-roots.epher -- expand (x - r1)(x - r2)(x - r3)

Vieta's formulas (Francois Viete, 1591; any algebra text) read the
coefficients of a monic polynomial off the roots: for three roots the
coefficient of x^2 is -(r1 + r2 + r3), of x is r1 r2 + r1 r3 + r2 r3, and
the constant is -r1 r2 r3. With roots 1, 2 and 3 that gives the running
cubic x^3 - 6x^2 + 11x - 6, then both forms are evaluated at x = 4 and
compared. All values are exact.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/algebra/polynomials/polynomial-from-roots.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\algebra\polynomials\polynomial-from-roots.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/algebra/polynomials/polynomial-from-roots.epher

The knobs to edit are the roots r1, r2 and r3 below.
============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs ---------------------------------------------------------------
const r1 = 1
const r2 = 2
const r3 = 3

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
// the elementary symmetric sums of the roots (Vieta)
e1 = r1 + r2 + r3                // echoes 6
e2 = r1 * r2 + r1 * r3 + r2 * r3 // echoes 11
e3 = r1 * r2 * r3                // echoes 6
cs = {1, -e1, e2, -e3}           // p(x) = x^3 - 6x^2 + 11x - 6 (echoes the list)
print("product form at x = 4:", (4 - r1) * (4 - r2) * (4 - r3))
print("expanded form at x = 4:", 4 ^ 3 + cs[2] * 4 ^ 2 + cs[3] * 4 + cs[4])
print("both forms agree:", (4 - r1) * (4 - r2) * (4 - r3) == 4 ^ 3 + cs[2] * 4 ^ 2 + cs[3] * 4 + cs[4])
/* ---- expected output ----
= 1
= 2
= 3
= 6
= 11
= 6
= {1, -6, 11, -6}
= product form at x = 4: 6
= expanded form at x = 4: 6
= both forms agree: true
*/
